# Certificate test data. Place at testdata/certs/.gitattributes.
# Patterns without a slash match at any depth, so these cover every combination
# subdirectory under valid/ and invalid/.

# OpenSSL writes LF; keep it that way on every platform so the bytes on disk match the
# bytes that were committed. bundle.pem is a literal concatenation of cert.pem and
# cert.pkey.pem, so a CRLF working copy breaks byte-exact comparisons. `text` also
# normalises on commit, which self-heals a CRLF copy added from a Windows checkout.
*.pem text eol=lf

# Never three-way merge generated key material: merging base64 produces a corrupt PEM
# that still looks structurally plausible. Resolve conflicts by regenerating.
*.pem -merge
